        {
            "depends_on": "eval:doc.enable_document_parsing && doc.parser_strategy === 'OCR Only'",
            "description": "A Python regex with named capture groups to extract address fields from the document text.\n\nEach group name becomes a field key in the extracted result.\n\nExample:\n  (?P\\d+).*?(?P[^\\n]+).*?(?P[^\\n]+)\n\nFor bilingual documents, suffix group names with the language:\n  (?P[^\\n]+)   \u2192 used when OCR Language is Arabic\n  (?P[^\\n]+)   \u2192 used when OCR Language is English\n  (?P\\d+)    \u2192 no suffix, always kept\n\nUse the \u201cLoad Country Template\u201d button to prefill a template for your country.\nLeave empty to show raw extracted text only.",
